hat height are<jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/xlink\" mime-subtype=\"png\" mimetype=\"image\" xlink:href=\"S0424820100074422_inline2.png\" \/>possible.<\/jats:p><jats:p>A step that ends at a screw dislocation must be of<jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/xlink\" mime-subtype=\"png\" mimetype=\"image\" xlink:href=\"S0424820100074422_inline2.png\" \/>high, corresponding to one unit cell in the (110) direction. Consequently, a<jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/xlink\" mime-subtype=\"png\" mimetype=\"image\" xlink:href=\"S0424820100074422_inline1.png\" \/>step must show lighter contrast than the one that ends at a screw dislocation, provided that the imaging conditions are the same for both. This result is shown in Fig. 1.a. Step 1 ends at a screw dislocation; therefore, step 2, which is lighter, must be one atom high.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/s0424820100074422","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T12:06:51Z","timestamp":1592482011000},"page":"110-111","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":2,"title":["Reflection electron microscopy (REM) observation of monatomic steps and &lt;133&gt; steps of GaAs(110) surfaces"],"prefix":"10.1017","volume":"41","author":[{"given":"Tung","family":"Hsu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"56","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0424820100074422_ref04","unstructured":"4. Hsu, Tung and Cowley, J.M. , to be published in Ultramicroscopy."},{"key":"S0424820100074422_ref01","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"450","DOI":"10.1017\/S0424820100054728","author":"Hsu","year":"1982","journal-title":"Proceedings, 40th Annual Meeting of Electron Microscopy Society of America"},{"key":"S0424820100074422_ref05","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1149\/1.2134108"},{"key":"S0424820100074422_ref03","doi-assert